{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c3a67cd2-60f3-4b9f-9cc0-487df4ef7756","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have resolved the issue and documented the fix in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-dOiITX/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of What Was Changed and Why\n- **Change**: In [`gen.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dOiITX/gen.py#L10-L13), changed the lower-bound field name from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"` in `hr_target()`:\n  ```python\n  def hr_target(step):\n      \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n      lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n      return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n  ```\n- **Why**: In Intervals.icu's workout JSON schema for FIT export to Garmin, `{units: \"%lthr\", value, end}` routes as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, which makes Garmin clamp the corridor to its own internal zone boundaries. Changing the key to `{units: \"%lthr\", start, end}` switches the FIT export mode to an Instant-HR target, which exports the exact computed bpm corridor directly onto the watch.\n","duration_seconds":42.23863,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":127098,"output_tokens":1416,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":61281,"total_tokens":128514}}}
